    "text": "Structure of butan-2-ol is<br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><munder><mrow><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow></munder><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math><br /><br />Now, the simple format of HBO (hydroboration oxidant) reaction is<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mtext>R</mtext><mo>−</mo><mtext>CH</mtext><mo>=</mo><msub> <mrow> <mtext>CH</mtext></mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>+</mo><msub> <mtext>B</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mn>6</mn> </msub> <mover> <mo>→</mo> <mrow> <mtext> </mtext><mtext>THF</mtext><mtext> </mtext></mrow> </mover> <msub> <mrow> <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mtext>R</mtext><mo>−</mo><msub> <mrow> <mtext>CH</mtext></mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>CH</mtext></mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow> <mn>3</mn> </msub> <mtext>B</mtext><mover> <mo>→</mo> <mrow> <mtext> </mtext><msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <msub> <mtext>O</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>/</mo><mover> <mtext>O</mtext> <mo>−</mo> </mover> <mtext>H</mtext><mtext> </mtext></mrow> </mover> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>RCH</mtext></mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <munder> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>CH</mtext></mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mrow> <mover> <mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" mathsize=\"140%\"><mrow> <mtext>OH</mtext></mrow></mstyle> <mo>|</mo> </mover> </mrow> </munder> </mrow> </math><br /><br />So, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> definitely an option as the mechanistic approach for the <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> addition is as<br /><br /><img src=\"assets\\st0089_a043539826d9.jpeg\" /><br /><br /><math> <mrow>  <msub>   <mrow>    <mo stretchy='false'>(</mo><msub>     <mrow>      <mtext>CH</mtext></mrow>     <mn>3</mn>    </msub>    <msub>     <mrow>      <mtext>CH</mtext></mrow>     <mn>2</mn>    </msub>    <mo>&#x2212;</mo><msub>     <mrow>      <mtext>CHCH</mtext></mrow>     <mn>3</mn>    </msub>    <mo stretchy='false'>)</mo></mrow>   <mn>3</mn>  </msub>  <mtext>B</mtext><mover>   <mo>&#x2192;</mo>   <mrow>    <mtext>&#x2003;</mtext><msub>     <mtext>H</mtext>     <mn>2</mn>    </msub>    <msub>     <mtext>O</mtext>     <mn>2</mn>    </msub>    <mo>/</mo><mover>     <mtext>O</mtext>     <mo>&#x2212;</mo>    </mover>    <mtext>H</mtext><mtext>&#x2003;</mtext></mrow>  </mover>  <msub>   <mrow>    <mtext>CH</mtext></mrow>   <mn>3</mn>  </msub>  <msub>   <mrow>    <mtext>CH</mtext></mrow>   <mn>2</mn>  </msub>  <mo>&#x2212;</mo><munder>   <mrow>    <munder>     <mtext>C</mtext>     <mo>&#x007C;</mo>    </munder>    <mtext>H</mtext></mrow>   <mrow>    <mtext>OH</mtext></mrow>  </munder>  <msub>   <mrow>    <mtext>CH</mtext></mrow>   <mn>3</mn>  </msub>  </mrow></math><br /><br />Now, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> can have both cis and trans-forms."
